      "html": "<section class=\"ds-dialog\" aria-label=\"Find existing profiles\"><h2 class=\"ds-dialog-title\">Find existing profiles</h2><p class=\"ds-dialog-body\">Add profiles already on this computer.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-dialog{width:430px;max-width:100%;border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--ink,#292933);box-shadow:0 20px 70px rgba(15,15,25,.22);font-family:Segoe UI,sans-serif}.ds-dialog-title{margin:0;padding:20px 25px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#e4e2df);font-size:19px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-dialog-body{margin:0;padding:24px 26px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted,#72717b)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A compact Windows utility",
    "overview": "Chromatic is a Windows Electron application with a React-rendered interface for Chromium browser profiles. Its established direction is quiet and practical: warm neutral surfaces, ink typography, restrained violet selection, and Segoe UI. Density supports finding and launching a browser identity quickly. The manager and hotkey popup share identity cues and controls.\n\nThe library uses aligned rows, an unobtrusive navigation rail, and a focused editor at the right edge. Tonal separation carries ordinary hierarchy; shadows identify temporary layers. Preserve this native-feeling utility direction when extending the application.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Search-first navigation and visible keyboard focus.",
      "Warm light neutrals and coordinated dark surfaces.",
      "Aligned profile rows with initials, browser names, and multiple labels.",
      "Restrained accent, compact controls, and a full-height side editor."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Paired Theme Rule",
        "body": "Change light and dark roles together; use semantic variables rather than placing light-only colors on application surfaces.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use semantic paired theme variables for all application surfaces and text.",
      "**Do** preserve the aligned library rows, right-side editor, and search-first launcher.",
      "**Do** keep keyboard focus, active-result semantics, and reduced-motion support visible in future work.",
      "**Do** use the original application icon and Lucide interface glyphs consistently.",
      "**Do** state concrete outcomes, preserved browser data, and actionable empty states."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn the compact utility into a marketing page or replace the library with dashboard cards.",
      "**Don't** expose hidden profiles in the launcher after manager PIN reveal.",
      "**Don't** style PIN access as browser-data encryption or promise indefinite website sessions.",
      "**Don't** imply scheduled cleanup or obscure the manual cache preview and confirmation."
    ]
  }
}
